  "notes": "CONJUGATION (godan-su):\n- Negative: {投|な}げ{出|だ}さない\n- Te-form: {投|な}げ{出|だ}して\n- Past: {投|な}げ{出|だ}した\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. Takes を for the thing being thrown out or abandoned.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {足|あし}を{投|な}げ{出|だ}す: to stretch out one's legs\n- {仕事|しごと}を{投|な}げ{出|だ}す: to abandon one's work\n- {責任|せきにん}を{投|な}げ{出|だ}す: to abandon responsibility\n- {途中|とちゅう}で{投|な}げ{出|だ}す: to quit halfway\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 2 carries a negative connotation of irresponsibility. Often used in criticism or self-criticism.",
